// Ember Clans roster: every building, unit, summon, hero and Honor Edict, with
// first-pass numbers. Design data for Conquest (M3): the game does not read
// this file yet. Readable copy and rationale: docs/17-unit-rosters.md.
//
// Each `stats` block uses exactly the fields of a data/units.ron entry (see
// the comment at the top of that file) so it can move into the game
// unchanged; tools/gc_bake/tests/rosters.rs bakes every block to prove it.
//
// Building fields (docs/21-buildings.md): name, role (Main, Outpost, Housing,
// Economy, Production, Tech, Heroes, Defence, Wall), tier (the main-building
// tier needed to build it), upgrades_from (main-building tiers 2 and 3:
// Some(the building it upgrades), with the upgrade's cost and time), cost,
// build_time (seconds at Standard tempo), hp, armour (Fortified, Structure,
// Living), footprint (tiles across and deep), supply (cap it adds), flags
// (DropOffGrub, DropOffMarrow, PowersField, AntiAir), attack (towers: range in
// tiles, damage per shot, seconds between shots, shots per volley) and effect
// (plain words). starting_buildings are what a player starts Conquest with
// (docs/04-economy.md). A unit's `from: Building("...")` names one of these
// buildings.
//
// Unit fields: tier (1 to 3; 0 for summoned units), class, cost (Grub and
// Marrow), supply, train_time (seconds; for Brood evolutions the cocoon
// time), from (Building("..."), Evolves("parent") or Summoned("by what")),
// flags, abilities, stats.
//
// Ability fields: name, kind (Passive, Aura, Toggle, Active, Autocast,
// Order, Ultimate), effect (plain words; hero ranks written 1/2/3), primitives (the
// effect primitives it would be built from), and where they apply cooldown
// (s), range (tiles), radius (tiles), duration (s). Meter abilities add cost
// (meter points) and tier.
